 ## Background
-Originated in the context of "NeRF in the Wild" (NeRF-W), where unconstrained photo collections contain transient objects like people and vehicles [S1]. The technique was introduced to address the inconsistency and non-smooth geometries that arise when standard NeRF models try to fit these transient objects as part of the static scene [S1]. It is a component of the Aug-NeRF framework, which injects worst-case perturbations into the NeRF pipeline [Parent].
+Originated in the context of "NeRF in the Wild" (NeRF-W), where unconstrained photo collections contain transient objects like people and vehicles [S1]. The technique was introduced to test model robustness to in-the-wild occlusions, as standard image comparison metrics are unable to ignore transient objects [S1]. It is a component of the Aug-NeRF framework, which injects worst-case perturbations into the NeRF pipeline [Aug-NeRF](10294-aug-nerf.md).
 
